{{Wireless adapter |brand=Wistron NeWeb |model=DNUR-S1 |revision= |upc= |ean= |asin= |price= |est_release_date= |fcc_date=07/20/2011 |manuf_country= |is_manuf=No |manuf= |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |availability= |if=USB (non-standard connector) |if_bus_version=2.0 |if_connector_type= |form_factor= |vendor_id= |device_id= |subvendor_id= |subdevice_id= |id_string= |fcc_id=A3LDNURS1 |ic_id=649E-DNURS1 |chip1_brand=Ralink |chip1_model=RT5370;RT5370N, P4P4660609, 1052ATA1; |chip2_brand= |chip2_model= |chip3_brand= |chip3_model= |chip4_brand= |chip4_model= |addl_chips= |accessible_UART=No |flags= |ant_conn= |802dot11_protocols=bgn |txchains=1 |rxchains=1 |sstreams=1 |oui=90:A4:DE |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} This module is '''Samsung''' P/N AK59-00131A. It would appear to be used with some of their Blu-ray players.
"2011/02/11", ""48DNUR08.SGD", and "RT5370-V20" is silkscreened on the back of the FCC EUT's board. :"2011/03/07", ""48DNUR08.0GA", and "RT5370-V20" is silkscreened on the back of a production model board.
